# WERDU.DE - PROJECT CONTEXT & INSTRUCTIONS

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW & ARCHITECTURE
- Website Domain: https://werdu.de
- Environment: WordPress environment located in `/httpdocs`.
- Primary Business Model: Direct-to-consumer sales of home battery storage systems (Heimspeicher / LiFePO4 batteries) in Germany. Transparent pricing is available directly on the site.
- Primary Goal: Achieve #1 Rankings, top conversion rates, and dominate AI Search (AIO / GEO - ChatGPT Search, Perplexity, Google SGE/AIO) for home energy storage in Germany (2026).

## 2. CALCULATORS & LEAD FLOW ARCHITECTURE
We have 3 Calculators on the site:
1. Calculator 1 (Main/Detailed): https://werdu.de/solarbatterie-rechner/
2. Calculator 2 (Homepage Preview/Quick): https://werdu.de/
3. Calculator 3 (Gratis Online Rechner): https://werdu.de/gratis-heimspeicher-rechner-online/

Flow Requirements:
- Calculators MUST NOT generate individual automated PDF quotes or formal price quotes, as transparent prices are already listed online in `/shop/`.
- Calculator output MUST redirect or pass parameters directly to the consultation page: `https://werdu.de/beratung-anfragen/`.
- On `https://werdu.de/beratung-anfragen/`, the user's calculated parameters (e.g., consumption, PV size, recommended kWh capacity) MUST pre-fill into the lead contact form so the customer can submit their details.
- Calculator 2 (Homepage) and Calculator 3 MUST act as quick previews and seamlessly pass parameters (via URL query parameters or session storage) to Calculator 1 or directly to `https://werdu.de/beratung-anfragen/`.

## 3. NEW FEATURE: LOCAL INSTALLER OPTION
- We do not issue complex custom quotes, but we are implementing an optional Installer Shipping & Setup Option.
- Option Details: Customers can select an additional service fee (+150€ to +300€).
- Mechanics: When selected, the battery is shipped directly to the nearest certified local installer. Upon delivery, the installer handles the physical installation at the customer's house.
- UX Integration: Integrate this choice clearly on product pages, checkout (`/kasse/`), and inside the consultation flow (`/beratung-anfragen/`).

## 4. SEO & AIO (AI OPTIMIZATION) STRICT GUIDELINES
- All PHP, JS, CSS, and HTML modifications must comply with 2026 technical SEO and Generative Engine Optimization (GEO/AIO) standards.
- Structured Data (JSON-LD): Implement/verify `SoftwareApplication`, `FAQPage`, `HowTo`, `Product`, `LocalBusiness` / `Service`, and `BreadcrumbList`. Ensure JSON-LD includes `areaServed` where applicable.
- Answer Engine Optimization (AIO): Use clear Answer-First (BLUF - Bottom Line Up Front) formatting in headers (H2/H3) and introductory paragraphs so AI crawlers can extract direct answers.
- Performance: Code must be optimized for Core Web Vitals (no blocking scripts, clean isolation, modular CSS/JS).

## 5. STRICT CODE & EXECUTION RULES FOR CURSOR
- NEVER remove existing core functionality without replacement.
- DO NOT invent non-existent file paths or missing functions. Always inspect existing code files first.
- Maintain absolute isolation for calculator scripts (e.g., `#werdu-calc-isolated`) to avoid theme CSS/JS conflicts.
- Ensure all German text produced is grammatically flawless, natural, and highly professional.
- Do not leave unfinished TODO comments in production code.

